{
    "name": "Oʻahu",
    "group": "Entity Cloud",
    "description": "The island of Oʻahu at 1:1: its real ground (AWS Terrain Tiles, 36 m cells, cut to OpenStreetMap's coastline), its 6,800 km of mapped roads with rounded curves, bridges and US markings, and its 97,000 mapped buildings stood up from their footprints, under trade-wind weather. Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL); made by tools/geo-import.mjs.",
    "entities": [
        {"type":"cloud","name":"Oʻahu"},
        {
            "type": "terrain", "size": 73728, "resolution": 2048, "base": -1.5, "rough": 1, "detail": 2, "style": "natural", "moisture": 0.75, "outside": "sea", "fieldSize": 805, "pivots": 0,
            "$comment": "1 m = 1 m: the 73.7 km square about 21.4835 N 157.9645 W (x east, z south), one cell per data cell, drawn smooth (bicubic) with vertices 1 m apart near the eye, coarser with distance (TerrainLod; detail 2: each lod reaches twice as far); rough: procedural detail of about a metre where the 36 m data is too coarse to hold it, more on steep ground, none on roads, buildings, the shore or water; natural ground (no farm sections or street grid; moisture: how green the open ground is, 0.5 by default), the sea round it to the horizon"
        },
        {"type":"curvature","radius":6371000},
        {
            "type": "render", "quality": 1, "shapeScale": 6000, "detailScale": 1100, "detailStrength": 0.55, "maxTop": 9000, "maxDistance": 80000,
            "weatherSize": 128000, "rainExtinction": 0.0024, "snowExtinction": 0.0036, "slant": 0.08, "fallSpeed": 40, "timeScale": 20, "particles": 24000
        },

        {"$comment":"the island: its ground and land cover, roads, buildings and place names (scenarios/data/oahu/: node tools/geo-import.mjs oahu)"},
